      "description": "Watch Luton vs Notts County highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 22, 2026. Luton Town and Notts County faced off in a League One encounter that promised to test the tactical discipline of both sides. Supporters arrived expecting a closely contested match as both teams aimed to establish their rhythm early in the season. First Half Drama and Deadlock Broken The match on August 22, 2026 , began with a high level of physicality, as the referee was forced into his pocket early for Luka Smyth and George Johnston . The competitive nature of the midfield battle saw further cautions for Scott Robertson and Kal Naismith . In the 41st minute, the deadlock was finally broken. Luton earned a penalty, and Nahki Wells stepped up to calmly slot the ball home, giving the hosts the lead. However, the momentum shifted just before the break. In the first minute of stoppage time, Notts County struck back. Callum Roberts found space in the box to fire past the goalkeeper, ensuring the teams went into the interval on level terms at 1-1. The late strike breathed new life into the visitors ahead of a crucial second half. Second Half Sees Momentum Swings The intensity remained high following the restart, with Kasey Palmer and goalscorer Nahki Wells both receiving yellow cards. In the 60th minute, Notts County completed the turnaround. Nicholas Tsaroulla provided a perfectly weighted assist for Oliver Cooper , who finished clinically to put the away side 2-1 ahead. The goal sparked a series of substitutions as both managers looked to freshen up their lineups. Luton responded almost immediately. Substitute Callum Marshall made an instant impact, finding the back of the net in the 68th minute after being set up by Kasey Palmer . With the score tied at 2-2, the final twenty minutes were a frantic affair. Despite late bookings for Liam Walsh and Hindolo Mustapha in the 93rd minute, neither side could find a winning goal before the final whistle blew after five minutes of added time."
