      "description": "Watch Notts County vs Leicester highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. Notts County and Leicester faced off in a highly anticipated League One fixture that promised intensity from the opening whistle. Both sides looked to establish their dominance early in the campaign on a crucial matchday. Early Tension and Tactical Discipline On August 15, 2026 , the match began as a cagey affair with both teams prioritizing defensive solidity. The physical nature of the contest was evident early on, as the referee reached for his pocket in the 15th minute to book Jack Evans of Notts County . As the first half drew to a close, the game grew increasingly fractious. James Gibbons received a yellow card in the 43rd minute, and he was quickly followed into the book by Leicester's Will Alves just moments before the halftime whistle. The Breakthrough and Strategic Shifts The second half saw a significant shift in momentum as both managers looked to influence the outcome. In the 62nd minute, the deadlock was finally broken. Sammy Braybrooke turned provider with a precise pass to Jayden Joseph , who clinical finish put Leicester into the lead. This sparked an immediate response from the Notts County dugout, as they introduced a triple substitution in the 67th minute, bringing on Conor Grant , Hindolo Mustapha , and Emile Acquah to rejuvenate their attacking options. Late Drama and the Impact of Substitutes The tactical gamble paid off handsomely for the home side. In the 81st minute, substitute Conor Grant found the back of the net to level the scores, rewarding the persistent pressure from Notts County . Despite a flurry of late changes, including the introduction of Hamza Choudhury and Tom Watson for Leicester , neither side could find a late winner. The referee blew the final whistle at 90+6' , bringing an end to a hard-fought contest where both teams shared the spoils."
